From 473d03035bc5b1c4b3e59e4d9cf00e6d963e2c5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stylianos Anastasiou <77302709+souvlakias@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:59:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] win32: winstore: re-apply the software gain when a stream
 starts

Volumes above 100% are applied as a session volume capped at 1 plus a
software gain requested with aout_GainRequest() in VolumeSet(). Every
new audio stream gets a fresh amplifier at unity gain from
aout_DecNew(), but Start() never requests the stored gain again, while
it still reports the previous volume to the core. After switching to the
next media, or after a decoder restart such as an audio track change,
playback above 100% is therefore quieter although the reported volume is
unchanged.

Request the stored gain once the stream has started, as mmdevice does at
the end of its Start().

Added for libvlc tag 3.0.23 (Screenbox issue #621).
---
 modules/audio_output/winstore.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/modules/audio_output/winstore.c b/modules/audio_output/winstore.c
index 5489349..a01ad7a 100644
--- a/modules/audio_output/winstore.c
+++ b/modules/audio_output/winstore.c
@@ -556,6 +556,7 @@ static int Start(audio_output_t *aout, audio_sample_format_t *restrict fmt)
 
     assert (sys->stream == NULL);
     sys->stream = s;
+    aout_GainRequest(aout, sys->gain);
     return 0;
 }
 
